This guide covers how to calculate and display trading metrics using the Orderly SDK hooks.

## Position Margin Calculation

Position margin is calculated as:

```
margin = Math.abs(positionSize) * markPrice * mmr
```

Where:
- `positionSize`: Positive for long, negative for short (use absolute value)
- `markPrice`: Current mark price
- `mmr`: Maintenance Margin Ratio

Position margin and value data can be obtained from `usePositionStream`:

```tsx
import { usePositionStream } from "@orderly.network/hooks";

const { positions } = usePositionStream();
// positions[].position_margin, positions[].position_value
```

## Current Leverage

Current leverage is calculated as:

```
currentLeverage = 1 / accountMarginRatio
```

Use the `useMarginRatio` hook:

```tsx
import { useMarginRatio } from "@orderly.network/hooks";

const { crossMarginRatio, crossAccountLeverage } = useMarginRatio();
```

### currentLeverage vs maxLeverage

| Property | Source | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `maxLeverage` | `useLeverage` | Maximum leverage the user can set for their account |
| `currentLeverage` | `useMarginRatio` | Computed based on open positions; changes dynamically |

To estimate leverage when placing a new order, use `useOrderEntry` which provides real-time data.

